Do not take PuTTY settings from an unsafe session.

PuttySettings may carry PuTTY keys that run a command when the session is
opened in PuTTY, so apply it only when the session is not unsafe, like the
other such settings. Carried as one line to keep the hunk's line count.

--- a/source/core/SessionData.cpp
+++ b/source/core/SessionData.cpp
@@ -983,1 +983,1 @@
-  PuttySettings = Storage->ReadString(L"PuttySettings", PuttySettings);
+  PuttySettings = Unsafe ? PuttySettings : Storage->ReadString(L"PuttySettings", PuttySettings);
